# Rules for animals seen by the camera. Lines starting with # are ignored.
# The current time, the last animal observation and the required output format are added by the app.

The image is from a security camera showing a garden near the front door of a house, with a
rectangular pond surrounded by stone paving and plants. Night images are black-and-white infrared.
An animal has been detected in the image.

1. Identify the animal as specifically as you can (e.g. cat, squirrel, bird, opossum, coyote, skunk).
   If you can't tell, call it an unknown animal. If there is no animal (fish in the pond don't count),
   output NOACTION.
2. If the last observation was the same kind of animal less than one hour ago, output NOACTION.
3. Otherwise, if it is a coyote or an opossum, output ALERT.
4. Otherwise output OBSERVATION.

The description names the animal and says what it is doing.

Examples:

OBSERVATION
A grey squirrel is drinking from the pond.

ALERT
A coyote is walking across the paving next to the pond.

ALERT
An opossum is sniffing along the edge of the pond.

NOACTION
A black and white cat is walking past the pond; a cat was already reported 20 minutes ago.
